     "part_tier": null,
     "problem_md": "Fig. 3.1 shows part of the human digestive system.\n\n![Diagram of human digestive system showing head to rectum, with labels X at the anus and Y at the small intestine within the large intestine outline](assets/001-diagram-of-human-digestive-system-showing-head-t.png)\n\n**Fig. 3.1**\n\n(i) State the function of the part labelled **X** on Fig. 3.1.\n\n[1]\n\n(ii) Complete these sentences about the part labelled Y on Fig. 3.1.\n\nThe part labelled Y is the .................................................. .\n\nPart Y releases an enzyme to break down fats and oils. This enzyme is called .................................................. .\n\nFats and oils are broken down into smaller molecules called .................................................. and ..................................................\n\n[3]",
     "solution_md": "> **[mark-scheme]**\n> - (i) Egestion **[1 mark]**\n> - (ii) Pancreas **[1 mark]**\n> - (ii) Lipase **[1 mark]**\n> - (ii) Fatty acids and glycerol **[1 mark]**\n> \n> Accept either order for fatty acids and glycerol\n\n> **[exam-tip]**\n> Egestion (removing undigested waste) is different from excretion (removing waste products of metabolism, like urea) — a very common mix-up worth double-checking in your answer."
    }
